  "text": "109. Consider the given statements.\n|. An immunity granted to a person from prosecution shall stand withdrawn if such person\nfails to pay any sum specified in the settlement order.\nIl. Settlement Commission cannot grant immunity from prosecution where the proceedings\nfor the prosecution have been instituted before the date of receipt of the application\nunder section 245C.\nIll. An immunity from prosecution once granted by the Settlement Commission cannot be\nwithdrawn on any ground.\nChoose the correct answer from the Code given below.\n(A) Only | is true.\n(B) | and Il are true but Ill is not true.\n(C) Il and III are true.\n(D) All are true.",
